  "selectionPolicy": {
    "direct": "Take the nearest front-facing intersection of body. A null mapping is intentionally not selectable, including face/head.",
    "forgiving": "On a miss, sample nearby screen rays within 22 CSS pixels and choose the closest visible hit. Prefer a visible projected joint anchor within 22 CSS pixels for joint selection; reject an anchor if a nearer body surface occludes it. Evaluate anchor triangle barycentrics on current morphed vertices. Provide a labeled area list as an accessible alternative.",
    "catchments": "Upper arms have separate biceps and triceps regions. Shoulder catchments cover deltoids; wrist catchments include hand and lower forearm. Calf includes the lower-leg surface. Hip includes the gluteal region.",
    "meaning": "Self-reported location only. No diagnosis, injured-muscle inference, or intensity-to-pathology mapping."
  },
